  "title": "Sum of All Odd Length Subarrays",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Prefix sum",
  "patterns": [
    "prefix sum"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "instead of summing subarrays one at a time, what if you asked: for a fixed element at index i, how many odd-length subarrays include it, and can you sum contributions per element instead?",
    "for index i (0-indexed), there are (i+1) choices for where a subarray could start at or before i, and (n-i) choices for where it could end at or after i - together giving total subarrays containing i",
    "half (rounded appropriately) of those subarrays have odd length - work out the exact odd count from the total count and the count starting before/after i",
    "multiply arr[i] by its odd-subarray count and sum over all i - this avoids ever materializing a subarray"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "miscounting how many subarrays containing index i have odd length versus even length",
    "double counting or missing subarrays that start and end exactly at i (length 1)",
    "reaching for the O(n) trick before getting a correct brute force first - verify against brute force on small inputs"
  ],
